&lt;p&gt;
brought a group of accomplished Asian basketball coaches to the United States for an exchange focused on coaching practice, player development, and high-performance training. The program began in Los Angeles, where the delegation attended NBA All-Star events at Intuit Dome, before continuing to the University of Missouri. At Mizzou, the group observed team practices and studied modern five-out offense, defensive principles, and strength and conditioning methods with the Tigers&amp;rsquo; coaching and performance staff.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Guests included UCBA representatives Enze Bai and Chairman
; Chinese national-team strength and conditioning coach and basketball commentator
; former China U15 women&amp;rsquo;s national-team coach and CUBA Guangzhou College of Applied Science and Technology men&amp;rsquo;s basketball head coach
; Singapore national-team assistant coach
and Indonesia National U18 Basketball Coach and SMA Jubilee Jakarta Head Coach
. The clinic concluded with a group visit to the Gateway Arch in St. Louis—a fitting final stop for a week built around learning, connection, and the shared language of basketball.&lt;/p&gt;
